      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did revert this already.\n\nIt takes longer because Gerrit seems to always serialize changes to the same file, even when they\u0027re in a relation chain together.  After separating the no-op cleanup, this CL showed as \"merge conflict\" - that\u0027s because of the cleanup CL editing the same file.  Thus no way to bundle the cleanup CL and the next CL in the same CQ run.  Sometimes CQ only takes a few hours, but often it takes days of retries to get past unrelated failures.\n\nI might be doing something wrong to cause the \"merge conflict\" status in these scenarios.  I\u0027m new to git and gerrit.",
